{"task_id": "Mbpp/6", "solution": "```python\ndef differ_At_One_Bit_Pos(num1: int, num2: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if two numbers differ at exactly one bit position.\"\"\"\n    xor_result = num1 ^ num2\n\n    set_bits_count = 0\n    while xor_result > 0:\n        xor_result &= (xor_result - 1)  # Clear the least significant set bit\n        set_bits_count += 1\n\n    return set_bits_count == 1\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/4", "solution": "```python\nimport heapq\n\ndef heap_queue_largest(numbers, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the n largest integers from a list of numbers and returns them in descending order.\n    Leverages the heapq module for efficient selection.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0 or not numbers:\n        return []\n\n    if n >= len(numbers):\n        return sorted(numbers, reverse=True)\n\n    largest_elements = heapq.nlargest(n, numbers)\n    return sorted(largest_elements, reverse=True)\n```\n"}
