{"task_id": "Mbpp/11", "solution": "```python\ndef remove_Occ(input_string: str, char_to_remove: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Removes the first and last occurrences of a specified character from an input string.\n\n    Handles cases where the character appears once or not at all.\n    \"\"\"\n    first_idx = input_string.find(char_to_remove)\n    last_idx = input_string.rfind(char_to_remove)\n\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        # Character not found at all\n        return input_string\n    elif first_idx == last_idx:\n        # Character found only once\n        return input_string[:first_idx] + input_string[first_idx + 1:]\n    else:\n        # Character found multiple times\n        # First remove the character at the last occurrence\n        string_after_last_removed = input_string[:last_idx] + input_string[last_idx + 1:]\n        # Then remove the character at the first occurrence (original index)\n        return string_after_last_removed[:first_idx] + string_after_last_removed[first_idx + 1:]\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/9", "solution": "```python\ndef find_Rotations(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the minimum number of rotations (greater than 0)\n    required for an input string to return to its original state.\n    Returns 0 if the input string is empty, as it cannot satisfy\n    the 'greater than 0' rotation constraint.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    temp_s = s\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        # Perform one cyclic shift.\n        temp_s = temp_s[1:] + temp_s[0]\n        if temp_s == s:\n            return i\n    # This line is a fallback; a string always returns to its original state after n rotations.\n    return n\n```"}
