{"task_id": "Mbpp/57", "solution": "```python\nimport functools\n\ndef find_Max_Num(digits: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the largest number that can be formed with the given list of digits.\n    This function uses a custom comparison logic to sort digits for concatenation.\n    \"\"\"\n    def compare(a, b):\n        str_a = str(a)\n        str_b = str(b)\n        if str_b + str_a > str_a + str_b:\n            return 1\n        elif str_b + str_a < str_a + str_b:\n            return -1\n        else:\n            return 0\n\n    if not digits or all(d == 0 for d in digits):\n        return 0\n\n    # Sort digits using the custom comparison.\n    sorted_digits = sorted(digits, key=functools.cmp_to_key(compare), reverse=False)\n\n    # Concatenate sorted digits to form the number.\n    largest_num_str = \"\".join(map(str, sorted_digits))\n\n    return int(largest_num_str)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/11", "solution": "```python\ndef remove_Occ(s: str, ch: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Removes the first and last occurrences of a given character from the string.\n    Returns the modified string or the original if the character is not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not s:\n        return \"\"\n\n    if len(s) == 1:\n        if s == ch:\n            return \"\"\n        else:\n            return s\n\n    first_idx = s.find(ch)\n\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        return s\n\n    last_idx = s.rfind(ch)\n\n    if first_idx == last_idx:\n        return s[:first_idx] + s[first_idx+1:]\n    else:\n        # Remove the first occurrence\n        temp_s = s[:first_idx] + s[first_idx+1:]\n\n        # Adjust the index for the last occurrence in the temporary string.\n        # If the original last_idx was after the removed first_idx, its new position shifts left by one.\n        new_last_idx = last_idx - 1\n\n        # Remove the adjusted last occurrence from the temporary string\n        return temp_s[:new_last_idx] + temp_s[new_last_idx+1:]\n\n```"}
