{"task_id": "Mbpp/63", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef max_difference(tuple_list: list) -> int | float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum absolute difference between elements in a list of numerical tuples.\n\n    Args:\n        tuple_list: A list of tuples, where each tuple contains exactly two numerical elements.\n\n    Returns:\n        The maximum absolute difference found.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If the input is not a list, or if any tuple is malformed\n                    (not a tuple, not of length 2, or contains non-numerical elements).\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(tuple_list, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n    if not tuple_list:\n        return 0.0\n\n    max_diff = -1.0\n\n    for i, tpl in enumerate(tuple_list):\n        if not isinstance(tpl, tuple) or len(tpl) != 2:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Element at index {i} is not a tuple of two elements: {tpl}\")\n\n        element1, element2 = tpl\n\n        if not isinstance(element1, (int, float)) or not isinstance(element2, (int, float)):\n            raise ValueError(f\"Elements in tuple at index {i} must be numerical: {tpl}\")\n\n        current_diff = math.fabs(element1 - element2)\n        if current_diff > max_diff:\n            max_diff = current_diff\n\n    return max_diff\n```\n"}
