{"task_id": "Mbpp/67", "solution": "```python\ndef bell_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the nth Bell number using Stirling numbers of the second kind.\n    It determines the number of ways to partition a set with 'n' elements into non-empty subsets.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # stirling[i][j] stores S(i, j), Stirling numbers of the second kind.\n    stirling = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # Base case: S(0, 0) = 1\n    stirling[0][0] = 1\n\n    # Calculate Stirling numbers S(i, j)\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            stirling[i][j] = stirling[i-1][j-1] + j * stirling[i-1][j]\n\n    # The nth Bell number B(n) is the sum of S(n, k) for k from 0 to n.\n    bell_n = 0\n    for j in range(n + 1):\n        bell_n += stirling[n][j]\n\n    return bell_n\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/69", "solution": "```python\ndef contains_sublist(main_list: list, sub_list: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a sublist is present contiguously within a main list.\n    An empty sublist is considered present in any main list.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(main_list)\n    m = len(sub_list)\n\n    if m == 0:\n        return True\n\n    if m > n:\n        return False\n\n    for i in range(n - m + 1):\n        if main_list[i:i+m] == sub_list:\n            return True\n\n    return False\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/68", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Union\n\ndef is_Monotonic(array: List[Union[int, float]]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if the given array (list) of numbers is monotonic.\n    Empty arrays and single-element arrays are considered monotonic.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(array) <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    is_increasing = True\n    for i in range(len(array) - 1):\n        if array[i] > array[i+1]:\n            is_increasing = False\n            break\n\n    is_decreasing = True\n    for i in range(len(array) - 1):\n        if array[i] < array[i+1]:\n            is_decreasing = False\n            break\n\n    return is_increasing or is_decreasing\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/68", "solution": "```python\ndef is_Monotonic(array: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an array is monotonically increasing, decreasing, or neither.\n    Returns True for empty or single-element arrays, as they are considered monotonic.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(array) <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    is_increasing = True\n    is_decreasing = True\n\n    for i in range(1, len(array)):\n        if array[i] < array[i-1]:\n            is_increasing = False\n        if array[i] > array[i-1]:\n            is_decreasing = False\n\n        # If it's neither increasing nor decreasing, we can short-circuit\n        if not is_increasing and not is_decreasing:\n            return False\n\n    return is_increasing or is_decreasing\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/67", "solution": "```python\ndef bell_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the nth Bell number using the Bell triangle method.\n    Returns the corresponding nth Bell number.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # Initialize a (n+1) x (n+1) 2D array for the Bell triangle.\n    bell = [[0 for _ in range(n + 1)] for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # Set the base case B_0 = 1.\n    bell[0][0] = 1\n\n    # Populate the Bell triangle row by row.\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        # The first element of the current row is the last element of the previous row.\n        bell[i][0] = bell[i - 1][i - 1]\n        # Calculate subsequent elements in the current row.\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            # Each element is the sum of the element to its left and the element diagonally above its left.\n            bell[i][j] = bell[i][j - 1] + bell[i - 1][j - 1]\n\n    # The nth Bell number is the first element of the nth row.\n    return bell[n][0]\n```\n"}
