{"task_id": "Mbpp/61", "solution": "```python\ndef count_Substrings(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts substrings where the sum of digits equals their length.\n    It iterates through all substrings, calculating their sum and length for comparison.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_count = 0\n    n = len(s)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i, n):\n            substring = s[i : j + 1]\n            current_length = len(substring)\n            current_sum_of_digits = _calculate_sum_of_digits(substring)\n\n            if current_sum_of_digits == current_length:\n                total_count += 1\n\n    return total_count\n\ndef _calculate_sum_of_digits(sub: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of digits for a given string of digits.\n    Each character digit is converted to an integer and added to a running sum.\n    \"\"\"\n    digit_sum = 0\n    for char_digit in sub:\n        digit_sum += int(char_digit)\n    return digit_sum\n```"}
