{"task_id": "Mbpp/72", "solution": "```python\ndef dif_Square(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if an integer can be represented as the difference of two squares (a\u00b2 - b\u00b2).\n    This is true if the number is odd or a multiple of 4; otherwise, it cannot be represented.\n    \"\"\"\n    # BR1: A number can be represented as the difference of two squares if it is odd.\n    if number % 2 != 0:\n        return True\n    # BR2: A number can be represented as the difference of two squares if it is a multiple of 4.\n    elif number % 4 == 0:\n        return True\n    # BR3: A number cannot be represented as the difference of two squares if it is even but not a multiple of 4.\n    else: # number is even but not a multiple of 4 (i.e., number % 2 == 0 and number % 4 != 0)\n        return False\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/74", "solution": "```python\ndef is_samepatterns(colors: list, patterns: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a list of colors follows a given pattern list with one-to-one mapping rules.\n    Returns True if a consistent one-to-one mapping exists, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(colors) != len(patterns):\n        return False\n\n    pattern_to_color_map = {}\n    color_to_pattern_map = {}\n\n    for i in range(len(patterns)):\n        pattern_char = patterns[i]\n        color = colors[i]\n\n        # Check pattern_char -> color mapping consistency\n        if pattern_char in pattern_to_color_map:\n            if pattern_to_color_map[pattern_char] != color:\n                return False\n        else:\n            pattern_to_color_map[pattern_char] = color\n\n        # Check color -> pattern_char mapping consistency\n        if color in color_to_pattern_map:\n            if color_to_pattern_map[color] != pattern_char:\n                return False\n        else:\n            color_to_pattern_map[color] = pattern_char\n\n    return True\n```"}
