{"task_id": "Mbpp/74", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Any, Dict\n\ndef is_samepatterns(sequence1: List[Any], sequence2: List[Any]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if two sequences follow a consistent one-to-one pattern mapping.\n    It returns True if patterns match, False otherwise due to length mismatch or mapping violation.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(sequence1) != len(sequence2):\n        # Mismatched lengths indicate different patterns.\n        return False\n\n    map1_to_2: Dict[Any, Any] = {} # Stores mapping from sequence1 elements to sequence2 elements.\n    map2_to_1: Dict[Any, Any] = {} # Stores mapping from sequence2 elements to sequence1 elements.\n\n    for i in range(len(sequence1)):\n        element1 = sequence1[i]\n        element2 = sequence2[i]\n\n        if element1 in map1_to_2:\n            if map1_to_2[element1] != element2:\n                # Returns False if element1 already maps to a different element2.\n                return False\n        else:\n            map1_to_2[element1] = element2\n\n        if element2 in map2_to_1:\n            if map2_to_1[element2] != element1:\n                # Returns False if element2 already maps to a different element1.\n                return False\n        else:\n            map2_to_1[element2] = element1\n\n    # All elements processed without violations, patterns match.\n    return True\n```"}
