{"task_id": "Mbpp/92", "solution": "```python\ndef is_undulating(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if an integer is \"undulating\" based on specific digit alternation rules.\n    This includes handling edge cases for single-digit and two-digit numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    num_str = str(number)\n    n = len(num_str)\n\n    if n == 1:\n        return True\n    elif n == 2:\n        return num_str[0] != num_str[1]\n    else: # n >= 3\n        # Verify digit[i] == digit[i+2]\n        for i in range(n - 2):\n            if num_str[i] != num_str[i+2]:\n                return False\n\n        # Verify digit[i] != digit[i+1]\n        for i in range(n - 1):\n            if num_str[i] == num_str[i+1]:\n                return False\n\n        return True\n```"}
