{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "```python\ndef eulerian_num(n, m):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the Eulerian number a(n, m).\n    It counts permutations of {1, ..., n} with exactly m ascents.\n    \"\"\"\n    def combinations(n_val, k_val):\n        \"\"\"Helper to calculate n_val choose k_val (binomial coefficient).\"\"\"\n        if k_val < 0 or k_val > n_val:\n            return 0\n        if k_val == 0 or k_val == n_val:\n            return 1\n        if k_val > n_val // 2:\n            k_val = n_val - k_val\n\n        res = 1\n        for i in range(k_val):\n            res = res * (n_val - i) // (i + 1)\n        return res\n\n    result = 0\n    for k in range(m + 1):\n        term = ((-1)**k) * combinations(n + 1, k) * ((m - k + 1)**n)\n        result += term\n    return result\n\n```"}
