{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "```python\ndef eulerian_num(n: int, m: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the Eulerian number a(n, m). This is the number of permutations of {1, ..., n} with exactly m ascents.\"\"\"\n\n    # Handle base cases where m is out of bounds or m is zero.\n    if m >= n or m < 0:\n        return 0\n    if m == 0 and n >= 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # Apply the recursive formula for other cases.\n    return (m + 1) * eulerian_num(n - 1, m) + (n - m) * eulerian_num(n - 1, m - 1)\n```"}
