{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "```python\ndef odd_Equivalent(s: str, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines the number of times a binary string, after specified left rotations,\n    represents an odd decimal number.\n    \"\"\"\n    odd_count = 0\n    current_s = s\n\n    for _ in range(n):\n        # A binary string is odd if its least significant bit (rightmost character) is '1'.\n        if current_s[-1] == '1':\n            odd_count += 1\n\n        # Perform a left rotation: move the first character to the end.\n        current_s = current_s[1:] + current_s[0]\n\n    return odd_count\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/111", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Any, Set\n\ndef common_in_nested_lists(nested_lists: List[List[Any]]) -> Set[Any]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds elements common to all sub-lists within a list of lists.\n    Returns a set of these common elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not nested_lists:\n        return set()\n\n    # Initialize common_set with elements from the first list.\n    common_set = set(nested_lists[0])\n\n    # Intersect with subsequent lists to find elements common to all.\n    for i in range(1, len(nested_lists)):\n        common_set = common_set.intersection(set(nested_lists[i]))\n        # Optimization: if common_set becomes empty, no more common elements can be found.\n        if not common_set:\n            break\n\n    return common_set\n```"}
