{"task_id": "Mbpp/125", "solution": "```python\ndef find_length(binary_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum difference between the count of '0's and '1's in any substring.\n    This implementation uses a variation of Kadane's algorithm.\n    \"\"\"\n    current_max = 0\n    global_max = 0\n\n    for char in binary_string:\n        if char == '0':\n            val = 1\n        else: # char == '1'\n            val = -1\n\n        current_max = max(val, current_max + val)\n        global_max = max(global_max, current_max)\n\n    return global_max\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/111", "solution": "```python\ndef common_in_nested_lists(nested_list: list[list]) -> set:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies and returns all elements present in every sublist of a given nested list.\n    Returns an empty set if no common elements are found or the input is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not nested_list:\n        return set()\n\n    # Initialize common_elements with the elements of the first sublist.\n    common_elements = set(nested_list[0])\n\n    # Iterate through the rest of the sublists and find the intersection.\n    for sublist in nested_list[1:]:\n        common_elements.intersection_update(set(sublist))\n        # If common_elements becomes empty, no further common elements exist.\n        if not common_elements:\n            break\n\n    return common_elements\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/125", "solution": "```python\ndef find_length(binary_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum difference between the count of '0's and '1's\n    in any contiguous substring of the given binary string.\n    The difference is defined as (count of '0's - count of '1's).\n    \"\"\"\n    if not binary_string:\n        return 0\n\n    # Transform the binary string: '0' becomes 1, '1' becomes -1.\n    # The problem then reduces to finding the maximum sum of a contiguous subarray.\n    transformed_array = [1 if char == '0' else -1 for char in binary_string]\n\n    # Apply Kadane's algorithm to find the maximum subarray sum.\n    # This variation correctly handles cases where all elements are negative.\n    max_so_far = transformed_array[0]\n    current_max = transformed_array[0]\n\n    for i in range(1, len(transformed_array)):\n        current_max = max(transformed_array[i], current_max + transformed_array[i])\n        max_so_far = max(max_so_far, current_max)\n\n    return max_so_far\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/126", "solution": "```python\ndef sum(num1: int, num2: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of all positive common divisors for two given positive integers.\n    It identifies divisors for each number, finds their intersection, and sums them.\n    \"\"\"\n    divisors_num1 = set()\n    for i in range(1, num1 + 1):\n        if num1 % i == 0:\n            divisors_num1.add(i)\n\n    divisors_num2 = set()\n    for i in range(1, num2 + 1):\n        if num2 % i == 0:\n            divisors_num2.add(i)\n\n    common_divisors = divisors_num1.intersection(divisors_num2)\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    for divisor in common_divisors:\n        total_sum += divisor\n    return total_sum\n```"}
