{"task_id": "Mbpp/131", "solution": "```python\ndef _is_vowel(char: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a character is a vowel (a, e, i, o, u, case-insensitive).\n    'y' is not considered a vowel for this function.\n    \"\"\"\n    return char.lower() in {'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u'}\n\ndef reverse_vowels(input_string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Reverses only the vowels within a given input string.\n    Non-vowel characters remain in their original positions.\n    \"\"\"\n    char_list = list(input_string)\n    vowel_indices = []\n    vowel_chars = []\n\n    for i, char in enumerate(char_list):\n        if _is_vowel(char):\n            vowel_indices.append(i)\n            vowel_chars.append(char)\n\n    vowel_chars.reverse()\n\n    for i, original_vowel_index in enumerate(vowel_indices):\n        char_list[original_vowel_index] = vowel_chars[i]\n\n    return \"\".join(char_list)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/126", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef sum(num1: int, num2: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of all positive common divisors for two given integers.\n    This leverages the property that common divisors of two numbers are the divisors of their greatest common divisor.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Determine the greatest common divisor (GCD) of the two input numbers.\n    # math.gcd handles inputs including zero correctly, where gcd(0, x) is abs(x) and gcd(0, 0) is 0.\n    gcd_val = math.gcd(num1, num2)\n\n    # If the GCD is 0 (meaning both num1 and num2 were 0),\n    # return 0 as there are no finite positive common divisors to sum.\n    if gcd_val == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    # Iterate through possible positive divisors up to the absolute value of the GCD.\n    for i in range(1, abs(gcd_val) + 1):\n        if abs(gcd_val) % i == 0:\n            total_sum += i\n\n    return total_sum\n```"}
