{"task_id": "Mbpp/141", "solution": "```python\ndef pancake_sort(input_list):\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of numbers in ascending order using the pancake sort algorithm.\"\"\"\n    current_list = list(input_list)\n    n = len(current_list)\n\n    def _flip(arr, k):\n        \"\"\"Reverses the prefix of the list from index 0 up to index k.\"\"\"\n        start = 0\n        while start < k:\n            arr[start], arr[k] = arr[k], arr[start]\n            start += 1\n            k -= 1\n\n    for current_size in range(n, 1, -1):\n        # Find the index of the maximum element in the current unsorted sub-list.\n        max_idx = 0\n        for i in range(1, current_size):\n            if current_list[i] > current_list[max_idx]:\n                max_idx = i\n\n        # If the maximum element is not already at its correct position.\n        if max_idx != current_size - 1:\n            # Flip the prefix to bring the maximum element to the front.\n            _flip(current_list, max_idx)\n            # Flip the entire current unsorted sub-list to move max to its sorted position.\n            _flip(current_list, current_size - 1)\n\n    return current_list\n```\n"}
