{"task_id": "Mbpp/141", "solution": "```python\ndef _flip(arr: list[int | float], k: int) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Reverses the order of the first k elements in the list.\n    Modifies the list in-place.\n    \"\"\"\n    arr[:k] = arr[:k][::-1]\n\ndef _find_max_index(arr: list[int | float], n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the index of the maximum element within the first n elements of the list.\n    Returns the index of the maximum element found.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_val = arr[0]\n    max_idx = 0\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        if arr[i] > max_val:\n            max_val = arr[i]\n            max_idx = i\n    return max_idx\n\ndef pancake_sort(arr: list[int | float]) -> list[int | float]:\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of numbers in ascending order using the pancake sort algorithm.\n    Returns the sorted list.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    for current_size in range(n, 1, -1):\n        max_idx = _find_max_index(arr, current_size)\n        if max_idx != current_size - 1:\n            if max_idx != 0:\n                _flip(arr, max_idx + 1)\n            _flip(arr, current_size)\n    return arr\n```"}
