{"task_id": "Mbpp/170", "solution": "```python\ndef sum_range_list(numbers: list, start_index: int, end_index: int) -> (int | float):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of numbers within a specified inclusive range in a list.\n    Handles empty lists, out-of-bounds indices, and inverted ranges by returning 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not numbers:\n        return 0\n\n    list_length = len(numbers)\n\n    # Adjust start_index, ensuring it's not less than 0.\n    # If the adjusted start_index is out of bounds (>= list_length), the range is invalid.\n    adjusted_start_index = max(0, start_index)\n    if adjusted_start_index >= list_length:\n        return 0\n\n    # Adjust end_index, ensuring it's not greater than list_length - 1.\n    # If the adjusted end_index is out of bounds (< 0), the range is invalid.\n    adjusted_end_index = min(list_length - 1, end_index)\n    if adjusted_end_index < 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # If the adjusted start_index is greater than the adjusted end_index, the range is empty.\n    if adjusted_start_index > adjusted_end_index:\n        return 0\n\n    current_sum = 0\n    for i in range(adjusted_start_index, adjusted_end_index + 1):\n        current_sum += numbers[i]\n\n    return current_sum\n```"}
