{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "```python\ndef is_majority(array: list[int], n: int, element: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an element is a majority element in a sorted array.\n    A majority element occurs more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return False\n\n    # Find the index of the first occurrence of the element using binary search.\n    first_idx = -1\n    low = 0\n    high = n - 1\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if array[mid] == element:\n            first_idx = mid\n            high = mid - 1  # Try to find an earlier occurrence in the left half.\n        elif array[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:  # array[mid] > element\n            high = mid - 1\n\n    # If the element is not found, it cannot be a majority element.\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        return False\n\n    # Find the index of the last occurrence of the element using binary search.\n    last_idx = -1\n    low = 0  # Reset low for the second binary search.\n    high = n - 1  # Reset high for the second binary search.\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if array[mid] == element:\n            last_idx = mid\n            low = mid + 1  # Try to find a later occurrence in the right half.\n        elif array[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:  # array[mid] > element\n            high = mid - 1\n\n    # Calculate the total number of occurrences.\n    count = last_idx - first_idx + 1\n\n    # Determine if the count is greater than n/2.\n    return count > (n / 2)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Any\n\ndef _find_first_occurrence(arr: List[Any], n: int, x: Any) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the index of the first occurrence of element x in the sorted array arr.\n    It returns -1 if the element is not found, using a binary search approach.\n    \"\"\"\n    low, high = 0, n - 1\n    result = -1\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == x:\n            result = mid\n            high = mid - 1\n        elif arr[mid] < x:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else: # arr[mid] > x\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result\n\ndef _find_last_occurrence(arr: List[Any], n: int, x: Any) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the index of the last occurrence of element x in the sorted array arr.\n    It returns -1 if the element is not found, using a binary search approach.\n    \"\"\"\n    low, high = 0, n - 1\n    result = -1\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == x:\n            result = mid\n            low = mid + 1\n        elif arr[mid] < x:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else: # arr[mid] > x\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result\n\ndef is_majority(arr: List[Any], n: int, x: Any) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if element x is a majority element in the sorted array arr of length n.\n    A majority element occurs more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n    first_idx = _find_first_occurrence(arr, n, x)\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        return False\n\n    last_idx = _find_last_occurrence(arr, n, x)\n\n    count = last_idx - first_idx + 1\n    majority_threshold = n / 2.0\n\n    return count > majority_threshold\n```"}
