{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "```python\ndef even_bit_set_number(num: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets all bits at even positions (0, 2, 4, ...) in the input number `num` to 1.\n    Bits at odd positions are left unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Calculate the maximum bit position for the mask to cover num and potential next even bits.\n    max_bit_pos = max(1, num.bit_length() + 2)\n\n    mask = 0\n    # Iterate through even bit positions and set them in the mask.\n    for i in range(0, max_bit_pos, 2):\n        mask |= (1 << i)\n\n    # Perform a bitwise OR operation to set even bits in num.\n    return num | mask\n```"}
