{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Union\n\ndef max_sum(arr: List[Union[int, float]]) -> Union[int, float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence, which is first increasing and then decreasing.\n    Handles empty arrays (returns 0) and single-element arrays (returns the element's value).\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return arr[0]\n\n    # inc_sum[i] stores the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at arr[i]\n    inc_sum = list(arr)\n    # dec_sum[i] stores the maximum sum of a decreasing subsequence starting at arr[i]\n    dec_sum = list(arr)\n\n    # Calculate inc_sum array\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j] and inc_sum[i] < inc_sum[j] + arr[i]:\n                inc_sum[i] = inc_sum[j] + arr[i]\n\n    # Calculate dec_sum array\n    for i in range(n - 2, -1, -1):\n        for j in range(n - 1, i, -1):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j] and dec_sum[i] < dec_sum[j] + arr[i]:\n                dec_sum[i] = dec_sum[j] + arr[i]\n\n    # Find the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence\n    max_bitonic_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        current_bitonic_sum = inc_sum[i] + dec_sum[i] - arr[i]\n        if current_bitonic_sum > max_bitonic_sum:\n            max_bitonic_sum = current_bitonic_sum\n\n    return max_bitonic_sum\n```"}
