{"task_id": "Mbpp/259", "solution": "```python\ndef maximize_elements(test_tup1, test_tup2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Maximizes elements from two tuples of tuples element-wise.\n    It iterates through corresponding inner tuples, taking the maximum of each element.\n    \"\"\"\n    result_list = []\n    for inner_tup1, inner_tup2 in zip(test_tup1, test_tup2):\n        new_inner_tup = (max(inner_tup1[0], inner_tup2[0]), max(inner_tup1[1], inner_tup2[1]))\n        result_list.append(new_inner_tup)\n    return tuple(result_list)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/259", "solution": "```python\ndef maximize_elements(tuple1: tuple[tuple[int | float, int | float], ...],\n                      tuple2: tuple[tuple[int | float, int | float], ...]) \\\n                      -> tuple[tuple[int | float, int | float], ...]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Maximizes two tuples of tuples element-wise.\n\n    Args:\n        tuple1: The first input tuple of tuples, e.g., ((1, 3), (4, 5)).\n                Each inner tuple must contain two numbers.\n        tuple2: The second input tuple of tuples, e.g., ((6, 7), (3, 9)).\n                Each inner tuple must contain two numbers.\n\n    Returns:\n        A new tuple of tuples where each element is the maximum of the\n        corresponding elements from the input tuples, e.g., ((6, 7), (4, 9)).\n    \"\"\"\n    return tuple(\n        (max(t1[0], t2[0]), max(t1[1], t2[1]))\n        for t1, t2 in zip(tuple1, tuple2)\n    )\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/262", "solution": "```python\ndef split_two_parts(input_list: list, L: int) -> tuple[list, list]:\n    \"\"\"Splits a list into two parts based on an integer length L, returning a tuple of the sub-lists.\n    Handles edge cases for L=0 or L >= list length without mutating the original list.\"\"\"\n\n    list_length = len(input_list)\n\n    if L <= 0:\n        first_sub_list = []\n        second_sub_list = list(input_list) # Create a shallow copy\n    elif L >= list_length:\n        first_sub_list = list(input_list) # Create a shallow copy\n        second_sub_list = []\n    else:\n        first_sub_list = input_list[0:L]\n        second_sub_list = input_list[L:]\n\n    return (first_sub_list, second_sub_list)\n```"}
