{"task_id": "Mbpp/283", "solution": "```python\nimport collections\n\ndef validate(integer_input: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the frequency of each digit in an integer is less than or equal to the digit itself.\n    Returns True if this condition holds for all digits, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    num_str = str(integer_input)\n    digit_frequencies = collections.Counter(num_str)\n\n    for digit_char, frequency in digit_frequencies.items():\n        digit_value = int(digit_char)\n        if frequency > digit_value:\n            return False\n\n    return True\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/283", "solution": "```python\ndef validate(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the frequency of each digit in the integer is less than or equal to the digit itself.\n    This function processes the input number digit by digit to ensure the validation condition holds.\n    \"\"\"\n    s_number = str(number)\n    digit_frequencies = {}\n\n    for char_digit in s_number:\n        digit_frequencies[char_digit] = digit_frequencies.get(char_digit, 0) + 1\n\n    for char_digit, count in digit_frequencies.items():\n        digit_value = int(char_digit)\n        if count > digit_value:\n            return False\n\n    return True\n```"}
