{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "```python\ndef max_sub_array_sum_repeated(arr: list, n: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the largest sum of a contiguous subarray in the modified array\n    formed by repeating the given array k times.\n    \"\"\"\n    # The 'n' parameter is present in the signature as per the prompt, but not used directly\n    # as len(arr) provides the size.\n\n    if not arr:\n        return 0\n    if k <= 0:\n        return 0\n\n    def _kadane(current_arr: list) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the maximum subarray sum for a single array using Kadane's algorithm.\"\"\"\n        if not current_arr:\n            return 0\n\n        max_so_far = current_arr[0]\n        current_max = current_arr[0]\n\n        for i in range(1, len(current_arr)):\n            current_max = max(current_arr[i], current_max + current_arr[i])\n            max_so_far = max(max_so_far, current_max)\n\n        return max_so_far\n\n    max_sum_single_occurrence = _kadane(arr)\n    if k == 1:\n        return max_sum_single_occurrence\n\n    total_sum = sum(arr)\n\n    max_prefix_sum = 0\n    current_prefix_sum = 0\n    for x in arr:\n        current_prefix_sum += x\n        max_prefix_sum = max(max_prefix_sum, current_prefix_sum)\n\n    max_suffix_sum = 0\n    current_suffix_sum = 0\n    for x in reversed(arr):\n        current_suffix_sum += x\n        max_suffix_sum = max(max_suffix_sum, current_suffix_sum)\n\n    # Consider the array repeated twice to capture sums that cross the boundary once.\n    max_sum_two_occurrences = _kadane(arr + arr)\n\n    if total_sum < 0:\n        # If the total sum is negative, repeating the array more than twice\n        # will only decrease the sum. So, the max sum will be either from\n        # a single occurrence or from two occurrences.\n        return max(max_sum_single_occurrence, max_sum_two_occurrences)\n    else:\n        # If the total sum is positive, repeating the array multiple times\n        # can increase the sum. The maximum sum would be the maximum of:\n        # 1. Max sum within a single occurrence.\n        # 2. Max sum spanning across repetitions (suffix + (k-2)*total_sum + prefix).\n        # 3. Max sum from two occurrences (already covers some spanning cases).\n        return max(max_sum_single_occurrence, max_suffix_sum + (k - 2) * total_sum + max_prefix_sum)\n\n```"}
