{"task_id": "Mbpp/300", "solution": "```python\ndef _combinations(n: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the number of combinations (n choose k).\n    This is a private helper function.\n    \"\"\"\n    if k < 0 or k > n:\n        return 0\n    if k == 0 or k == n:\n        return 1\n    if k > n // 2: # Optimization C(n, k) = C(n, n-k)\n        k = n - k\n\n    res = 1\n    for i in range(k):\n        res = res * (n - i) // (i + 1)\n    return res\n\ndef count_binary_seq(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the count of binary sequences of length 2n where the sum of the first n bits equals the sum of the last n bits.\n    This function leverages the combinatorial identity sum_{k=0 to n} (C(n,k))^2 = C(2n, n).\n    \"\"\"\n    return _combinations(2 * n, n)\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef _kadane(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum contiguous subarray sum for a single array.\n    Returns 0 for an empty array.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not arr:\n        return 0\n\n    max_so_far = arr[0]\n    current_max = arr[0]\n\n    for i in range(1, len(arr)):\n        current_max = max(arr[i], current_max + arr[i])\n        max_so_far = max(max_so_far, current_max)\n\n    return max_so_far\n\ndef _total_sum(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of all elements in the array.\n    \"\"\"\n    return sum(arr)\n\ndef _max_prefix_sum(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum of a subarray starting from the beginning.\n    Returns 0 for an empty array.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not arr:\n        return 0\n\n    max_p_sum = float('-inf')\n    current_p_sum = 0\n\n    for x in arr:\n        current_p_sum += x\n        max_p_sum = max(max_p_sum, current_p_sum)\n\n    return max_p_sum\n\ndef _max_suffix_sum(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum of a subarray ending at the end.\n    Returns 0 for an empty array.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not arr:\n        return 0\n\n    max_s_sum = float('-inf')\n    current_s_sum = 0\n\n    for x in reversed(arr):\n        current_s_sum += x\n        max_s_sum = max(max_s_sum, current_s_sum)\n\n    return max_s_sum\n\ndef max_sub_array_sum_repeated(arr, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the largest sum of a contiguous subarray in a modified array\n    formed by repeating arr k times.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not arr or k == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    max_in_single = _kadane(arr)\n\n    if k == 1:\n        return max_in_single\n\n    total_array_sum = _total_sum(arr)\n    max_prefix = _max_prefix_sum(arr)\n    max_suffix = _max_suffix_sum(arr)\n\n    max_overall = max_in_single\n    max_overall = max(max_overall, max_suffix + max_prefix)\n\n    if total_array_sum > 0:\n        max_overall = max(max_overall, max_suffix + (k - 2) * total_array_sum + max_prefix)\n\n    return max_overall\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/299", "solution": "```python\ndef max_aggregate(input_list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of scores for each name and finds the name with the highest aggregate score.\n    Returns a tuple with the name and its total score.\n    \"\"\"\n    aggregated_scores = {}\n\n    for name, score in input_list:\n        aggregated_scores[name] = aggregated_scores.get(name, 0) + score\n\n    max_name = None\n    max_score = float('-inf') # Initialize with negative infinity to correctly handle all score values\n\n    for name, total_score in aggregated_scores.items():\n        if total_score > max_score:\n            max_score = total_score\n            max_name = name\n\n    return (max_name, max_score)\n```"}
