{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "```python\ndef max_sum_increasing_subseq(array: list[int], length: int, i: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence from array[0...i]\n    that includes array[k], where k > i.\n    \"\"\"\n    # dp[x] stores the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at index x.\n    dp = [0] * (i + 1)\n\n    for current_idx in range(i + 1):\n        dp[current_idx] = array[current_idx]\n        for prev_idx in range(current_idx):\n            if array[current_idx] > array[prev_idx]:\n                dp[current_idx] = max(dp[current_idx], dp[prev_idx] + array[current_idx])\n\n    max_prefix_sum = 0\n    for prefix_idx in range(i + 1):\n        if array[k] > array[prefix_idx]:\n            max_prefix_sum = max(max_prefix_sum, dp[prefix_idx])\n\n    return max_prefix_sum + array[k]\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/308", "solution": "```python\ndef _compute_all_products(list1, list2):\n    \"\"\"Computes all possible products by pairing elements from two lists.\"\"\"\n    products = []\n    for val1 in list1:\n        for val2 in list2:\n            products.append(val1 * val2)\n    return products\n\ndef _identify_n_largest(all_products, n):\n    \"\"\"Sorts products in descending order and returns the top n.\"\"\"\n    all_products.sort(reverse=True)\n    return all_products[:n]\n\ndef large_product(list1, list2, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the specified number of largest products from two given lists.\n    It returns the 'n' largest products, sorted in descending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    all_products = _compute_all_products(list1, list2)\n    n_largest_products = _identify_n_largest(all_products, n)\n    return n_largest_products\n```"}
