{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "```python\ndef max_sum_increasing_subseq(numbers: list[float | int], length: int, i: int, k: int) -> float | int:\\\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence from the prefix\n    up to index `i`, including the element at index `k`.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Initialize DP array: dp[j] stores max sum IS ending at numbers[j] (within prefix 0 to i)\n    dp = [0] * (i + 1)\n    for idx in range(i + 1):\\\n        dp[idx] = numbers[idx]\n\n    # Populate DP array for all elements up to index i\n    for current_idx in range(i + 1):\n        for prev_idx in range(current_idx):\n            if numbers[current_idx] > numbers[prev_idx]:\n                dp[current_idx] = max(dp[current_idx], dp[prev_idx] + numbers[current_idx])\n\n    # Find the maximum sum from dp[0...i] that can precede numbers[k]\n    max_prefix_sum = 0\n    for idx in range(i + 1):\n        if numbers[idx] < numbers[k]:\n            max_prefix_sum = max(max_prefix_sum, dp[idx])\n\n    # The final sum includes numbers[k] and the best preceding subsequence sum\n    return max_prefix_sum + numbers[k]\n```"}
