{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "```python\ndef set_left_most_unset_bit(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets the leftmost unset bit in the given integer.\n    Returns the integer with its leftmost unset bit set to 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # Find the index of the most significant bit.\n    # Iterate downwards from this position to find the leftmost unset bit.\n    msb_pos = number.bit_length() - 1\n    for bit_position in range(msb_pos, -1, -1):\n        if not ((number >> bit_position) & 1):\n            return number | (1 << bit_position)\n\n    # If all bits up to msb_pos are set, the next bit position is the leftmost unset.\n    return number | (1 << (msb_pos + 1))\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "```python\ndef set_left_most_unset_bit(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Sets the leftmost unset bit in an integer to 1.\n    Returns the modified integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    target_pos = -1\n    # Search for an unset bit from the most significant bit downwards,\n    # within the number's current binary representation length.\n    for i in range(n.bit_length() - 1, -1, -1):\n        if ((n >> i) & 1) == 0:\n            target_pos = i\n            break\n\n    # If no unset bit was found within the current bit length (e.g., n is 0b111),\n    # the leftmost unset bit is at the next highest position.\n    if target_pos == -1:\n        target_pos = n.bit_length()\n\n    return n | (1 << target_pos)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/389", "solution": "```python\ndef find_lucas(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the n'th Lucas number iteratively.\n    Handles base cases for n=0 and n=1, then iterates for n > 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 2\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 1\n    else:\n        a, b = 2, 1  # Initialize L(0) and L(1)\n        for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n            next_lucas = a + b\n            a = b\n            b = next_lucas\n        return b\n```"}
