{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "```python\n_memo = {}\n\ndef get_max_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum sum based on the recursive formula f(n) = max((f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n).\"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        return 0\n\n    if n in _memo:\n        return _memo[n]\n\n    sum_of_parts = (\n        get_max_sum(n // 2) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 3) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 4) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 5)\n    )\n\n    result = max(n, sum_of_parts)\n    _memo[n] = result\n    return result\n```"}
