{"task_id": "Mbpp/391", "solution": "```python\ndef convert_list_dictionary(list1, list2, list3):\n    \"\"\"\n    Transforms three input lists into a list of nested dictionaries.\n    Combines elements from the lists based on their corresponding indices.\n    \"\"\"\n    result_list = []\n    for outer_key, inner_key, inner_value in zip(list1, list2, list3):\n        inner_dict = {inner_key: inner_value}\n        outer_dict = {outer_key: inner_dict}\n        result_list.append(outer_dict)\n    return result_list\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "```python\ndef get_max_sum(n, _memo={}):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum for a given non-negative integer n using a specific recursive equation.\n    Employs dynamic programming with memoization for efficient computation.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n in _memo:\n        return _memo[n]\n\n    if n == 0:\n        _memo[n] = 0\n        return 0\n\n    # Calculate parts using integer division\n    sum_of_parts = (\n        get_max_sum(n // 2, _memo) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 3, _memo) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 4, _memo) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 5, _memo)\n    )\n\n    result = max(sum_of_parts, n)\n    _memo[n] = result\n    return result\n```"}
