{"task_id": "Mbpp/415", "solution": "```python\ndef max_Product(numbers: list[int]) -> tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds a pair of integers from an array that yields the highest product.\n    Handles arrays with fewer than two elements by raising a ValueError.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(numbers) < 2:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input array must contain at least two elements.\")\n\n    # Sort the array to easily identify the largest and smallest numbers.\n    sorted_numbers = sorted(numbers)\n\n    # The candidates for the highest product are:\n    # 1. The two largest positive numbers.\n    # 2. The two smallest (most negative) numbers.\n\n    # Identify the two largest numbers.\n    max1, max2 = sorted_numbers[-1], sorted_numbers[-2]\n\n    # Identify the two smallest numbers.\n    min1, min2 = sorted_numbers[0], sorted_numbers[1]\n\n    # Calculate products of candidate pairs.\n    product_of_max_two = max1 * max2\n    product_of_min_two = min1 * min2\n\n    # Return the pair that yields the highest product.\n    if product_of_max_two >= product_of_min_two:\n        return (max2, max1)  # Return in sorted order for consistency, per example (7,8) from (8,7)\n    else:\n        return (min1, min2)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/415", "solution": "```python\ndef max_Product(input_array: list[int]) -> tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"Finds the pair of integers with the highest product from the given array.\n    Returns a tuple containing the two integers whose product is the highest.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Sort the array to easily find the largest and smallest numbers.\n    # This handles positive, negative, and zero values efficiently.\n    sorted_array = sorted(input_array)\n    n = len(sorted_array)\n\n    # Case 1: Product of the two largest numbers.\n    product1 = sorted_array[n-1] * sorted_array[n-2]\n    pair1 = (sorted_array[n-1], sorted_array[n-2])\n\n    # Case 2: Product of the two smallest (most negative) numbers.\n    product2 = sorted_array[0] * sorted_array[1]\n    pair2 = (sorted_array[0], sorted_array[1])\n\n    if product1 >= product2:\n        return pair1\n    else:\n        return pair2\n```"}
