{"task_id": "Mbpp/428", "solution": "```python\ndef shell_sort(arr: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of numbers in ascending order using the Shell Sort algorithm.\"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    gap = n // 2  # Start with an initial large gap.\n\n    while gap > 0:  # Continue sorting as long as the gap is greater than 0.\n        for i in range(gap, n):\n            temp = arr[i]\n            j = i\n            while j >= gap and arr[j - gap] > temp:\n                arr[j] = arr[j - gap]\n                j -= gap\n            arr[j] = temp\n        gap //= 2  # Reduce the gap for the next pass through the list.\n    return arr\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/428", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Union\n\ndef shell_sort(input_array: List[Union[int, float]]) -> List[Union[int, float]]:\n    \"\"\"Sorts an array using the Shell Sort algorithm. Modifies the input array in-place.\"\"\"\n    n = len(input_array)\n\n    gap = n // 2  # Initialize the gap, reducing it by half in each pass.\n\n    while gap > 0:\n        # Perform a gapped insertion sort for the current gap.\n        for i in range(gap, n):\n            temp = input_array[i]\n            j = i\n            while j >= gap and input_array[j - gap] > temp:\n                input_array[j] = input_array[j - gap]\n                j -= gap\n            input_array[j] = temp\n        gap //= 2  # Reduce the gap for the next iteration.\n\n    return input_array\n```"}
