{"task_id": "Mbpp/440", "solution": "```python\nimport re\n\ndef _strip_punctuation(word: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Removes leading and trailing punctuation from a word.\"\"\"\n    # Common punctuation characters manually defined to avoid external imports.\n    PUNCTUATION = '!\\\"#$%&\\'()*+,-./:;<=>?@[\\\\]^_`{|}~'\n    return word.strip(PUNCTUATION)\n\ndef _is_adverb(word: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a word is likely an adverb based on a simple 'ly' suffix heuristic.\"\"\"\n    # This heuristic identifies words ending in 'ly' that are sufficiently long.\n    return len(word) > 2 and word.lower().endswith('ly')\n\ndef find_adverb_position(sentence: str) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first adverb and its exact character positions in a given sentence.\n    Returns a tuple (start_index, end_index, adverb_string) or (-1, -1, '') if no adverb is found.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Iterates through non-whitespace sequences (potential words) in the sentence.\n    for match in re.finditer(r'\\S+', sentence):\n        word_start_in_sentence = match.start()\n        word_with_punctuation = match.group(0)\n\n        cleaned_word = _strip_punctuation(word_with_punctuation)\n\n        if _is_adverb(cleaned_word):\n            # Calculate the exact start and end index of the cleaned adverb within the original sentence.\n            # This accounts for any leading punctuation that was stripped.\n            offset_in_token = word_with_punctuation.find(cleaned_word)\n            actual_adverb_start_index = word_start_in_sentence + offset_in_token\n            actual_adverb_end_index = actual_adverb_start_index + len(cleaned_word)\n\n            return (actual_adverb_start_index, actual_adverb_end_index, cleaned_word)\n\n    # Returns the 'not found' indicator if no adverb is identified.\n    return (-1, -1, '')\n```"}
