{"task_id": "Mbpp/448", "solution": "```python\ndef cal_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of Perrin numbers up to a given index n.\n\n    The Perrin sequence is defined as P(0)=3, P(1)=0, P(2)=2,\n    and P(n) = P(n-2) + P(n-3) for n > 2.\n\n    Args:\n        n: The maximum index (inclusive) up to which Perrin numbers should be summed.\n\n    Returns:\n        The sum of Perrin numbers from P(0) to P(n).\n    \"\"\"\n    _memo = {0: 3, 1: 0, 2: 2}\n\n    def get_perrin_number(index: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Returns the Perrin number at the specified index, using memoization.\n        \"\"\"\n        if index in _memo:\n            return _memo[index]\n\n        # Calculate recursively and store\n        result = get_perrin_number(index - 2) + get_perrin_number(index - 3)\n        _memo[index] = result\n        return result\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n + 1):\n        total_sum += get_perrin_number(i)\n    return total_sum\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/448", "solution": "```python\ndef cal_sum(n):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of the first n Perrin numbers (from P(0) to P(n) inclusive).\n    Perrin sequence: P(0)=3, P(1)=0, P(2)=2, P(k) = P(k-2) + P(k-3) for k > 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n\n    # Initialize the last three Perrin numbers needed for recurrence\n    p_prev_3 = 3  # Corresponds to P(0)\n    p_prev_2 = 0  # Corresponds to P(1)\n    p_prev_1 = 2  # Corresponds to P(2)\n\n    for i in range(n + 1):\n        if i == 0:\n            current_perrin = p_prev_3\n        elif i == 1:\n            current_perrin = p_prev_2\n        elif i == 2:\n            current_perrin = p_prev_1\n        else:\n            # Calculate the next Perrin number using the recurrence relation P(k) = P(k-2) + P(k-3)\n            current_perrin = p_prev_2 + p_prev_3\n            # Shift the previous values for the next iteration\n            p_prev_3 = p_prev_2\n            p_prev_2 = p_prev_1\n            p_prev_1 = current_perrin\n\n        total_sum += current_perrin\n\n    return total_sum\n```\n"}
