{"task_id": "Mbpp/556", "solution": "```python\ndef find_Odd_Pair(arr: list[int], n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts pairs in a list whose bitwise XOR results in an odd value.\n    It iterates through all unique pairs to perform this check.\"\"\"\n    odd_pair_count = 0\n\n    # Iterate through all unique pairs (arr[i], arr[j])\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            num1 = arr[i]\n            num2 = arr[j]\n\n            # Calculate the bitwise XOR of the pair\n            xor_result = num1 ^ num2\n\n            # Check if the XOR result is odd using bitwise AND with 1\n            if (xor_result & 1) == 1:\n                odd_pair_count += 1\n\n    return odd_pair_count\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/555", "solution": "def _calculate_sum_of_numbers(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of the first 'n' natural numbers using the direct formula.\"\"\"\n    return (n * (n + 1)) // 2\n\ndef _calculate_sum_of_cubes(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of the cubes of the first 'n' natural numbers using a formula.\"\"\"\n    sum_n = _calculate_sum_of_numbers(n)\n    return sum_n * sum_n\n\ndef difference(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the difference between the sum of cubes of the first 'n' natural numbers\n    and the sum of the first 'n' natural numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    sum_of_n = _calculate_sum_of_numbers(n)\n    sum_of_cubes_n = _calculate_sum_of_cubes(n)\n    return sum_of_cubes_n - sum_of_n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/556", "solution": "```python\ndef find_Odd_Pair(arr: list[int], n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts unique pairs in a list whose bitwise XOR results in an odd number.\n    Iterates through all pairs and checks the parity of their XOR sum.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            xor_result = arr[i] ^ arr[j]\n            if xor_result % 2 != 0:\n                count += 1\n    return count\n```"}
