{"task_id": "Mbpp/558", "solution": "```python\ndef digit_distance_nums(num1: int, num2: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of absolute differences between corresponding digits of two integers.\n    Shorter numbers are conceptually padded with leading zeros to match length.\"\"\"\n    str_num1 = str(num1)\n    str_num2 = str(num2)\n\n    max_len = max(len(str_num1), len(str_num2))\n\n    # Conceptual padding with leading zeros\n    padded_num1 = str_num1.zfill(max_len)\n    padded_num2 = str_num2.zfill(max_len)\n\n    total_difference = 0\n    for i in range(max_len):\n        digit1 = int(padded_num1[i])\n        digit2 = int(padded_num2[i])\n        total_difference += abs(digit1 - digit2)\n\n    return total_difference\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/559", "solution": "```python\ndef max_sub_array_sum(input_list: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of the largest contiguous sublist within the input list.\n    This implementation uses Kadane's algorithm to find the maximum sum.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_list:\n        return 0\n\n    max_so_far = input_list[0]\n    current_max = input_list[0]\n\n    for num in input_list[1:]:\n        current_max = max(num, current_max + num)\n        max_so_far = max(max_so_far, current_max)\n\n    return max_so_far\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/463", "solution": "def max_subarray_product(nums: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum product of a contiguous subarray within a given list of integers.\n    Handles empty lists, single elements, and lists with zeros or all negative numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not nums:\n        return 0\n\n    max_so_far = nums[0]\n    max_ending_here = nums[0]\n    min_ending_here = nums[0]\n\n    for i in range(1, len(nums)):\n        curr = nums[i]\n\n        # Store the old max_ending_here to use in min_ending_here calculation\n        temp_max = max_ending_here\n\n        # Current max product can be the current number itself, or current * max_ending_here, or current * min_ending_here\n        max_ending_here = max(curr, curr * temp_max, curr * min_ending_here)\n\n        # Current min product can be the current number itself, or current * max_ending_here, or current * min_ending_here\n        min_ending_here = min(curr, curr * temp_max, curr * min_ending_here)\n\n        # Update the global maximum product found so far\n        max_so_far = max(max_so_far, max_ending_here)\n\n    return max_so_far"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/559", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef max_sub_array_sum(arr, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of the largest contiguous sublist within the input list `arr`.\n    This function implements Kadane's algorithm to efficiently find the maximum subarray sum.\n    \"\"\"\n    current_max = 0\n    global_max = -math.inf # Initialized to negative infinity to handle all negative numbers\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        # Update current_max: either extend the previous subarray or start a new one.\n        current_max = max(arr[i], current_max + arr[i])\n        # Update global_max if the current subarray sum is greater.\n        global_max = max(global_max, current_max)\n\n    return global_max\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/558", "solution": "```python\ndef digit_distance_nums(num1: int, num2: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of the absolute differences between corresponding digits of two numbers.\n    It pads shorter numbers with leading zeros for alignment.\n    \"\"\"\n    str_num1 = str(num1)\n    str_num2 = str(num2)\n\n    max_length = max(len(str_num1), len(str_num2))\n\n    padded_num1_str = str_num1.zfill(max_length)\n    padded_num2_str = str_num2.zfill(max_length)\n\n    total_difference = 0\n\n    # Iterate from the rightmost digit to the leftmost digit.\n    for i in range(max_length - 1, -1, -1):\n        digit1 = int(padded_num1_str[i])\n        digit2 = int(padded_num2_str[i])\n\n        current_difference = abs(digit1 - digit2)\n        total_difference += current_difference\n\n    return total_difference\n```"}
