{"task_id": "Mbpp/572", "solution": "```python\nfrom collections import Counter\n\ndef two_unique_nums(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Removes duplicate numbers from a given list.\n    If a number appears more than once, all occurrences of that number are removed.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_list:\n        return []\n\n    # Count occurrences of each number in the list.\n    counts = Counter(input_list)\n\n    # Filter for numbers that appear exactly once.\n    unique_numbers = [num for num in input_list if counts[num] == 1]\n\n    return unique_numbers\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/572", "solution": "```python\ndef two_unique_nums(numbers: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Filters a list of numbers to return only those that appear exactly once, preserving their original order.\"\"\"\n    freq_counter = {}\n    for num in numbers:\n        freq_counter[num] = freq_counter.get(num, 0) + 1\n\n    unique_numbers_list = []\n    for num in numbers:\n        if freq_counter[num] == 1:\n            unique_numbers_list.append(num)\n\n    return unique_numbers_list\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/576", "solution": "```python\ndef is_Sub_Array(main_list: list, sub_list: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if sub_list is a contiguous sublist within main_list.\n    Returns True if found, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not sub_list:\n        return True\n    if not main_list or len(sub_list) > len(main_list):\n        return False\n\n    n = len(main_list)\n    m = len(sub_list)\n\n    for i in range(n - m + 1):\n        if main_list[i:i+m] == sub_list:\n            return True\n    return False\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/576", "solution": "```python\ndef is_Sub_Array(main_list: list, sub_list: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if 'sub_list' is a contiguous sublist of 'main_list'.\n    \"\"\"\n    # An empty list is always a sublist of any list.\n    if not sub_list:\n        return True\n\n    # A non-empty sublist cannot be found in an empty main_list.\n    if not main_list:\n        return False\n\n    n = len(main_list)\n    m = len(sub_list)\n\n    # If the sublist is longer than the main list, it cannot be a sublist.\n    if m > n:\n        return False\n\n    # Iterate through the main_list to find a matching slice.\n    for i in range(n - m + 1):\n        if main_list[i:i+m] == sub_list:\n            return True\n\n    return False\n```"}
