{"task_id": "Mbpp/573", "solution": "```python\nimport collections\n\ndef unique_product(numbers: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the product of numbers that appear exactly once in the input list.\n    Returns 1 if no such unique numbers exist (e.g., list is empty or all numbers are duplicates).\n    \"\"\"\n    counts = collections.Counter(numbers)\n    product = 1\n    for num, count in counts.items():\n        if count == 1:\n            product *= num\n    return product\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/577", "solution": "```python\ndef _calculate_factorial(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the factorial of a non-negative integer n.\n    Handles 0! = 1 and 1! = 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0 or n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    factorial_val = 1\n    for i in range(2, n + 1):\n        factorial_val *= i\n    return factorial_val\n\ndef last_Digit_Factorial(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the last digit of the factorial of n.\n    It uses a helper function to compute the full factorial first.\n    \"\"\"\n    factorial_value = _calculate_factorial(n)\n    return factorial_value % 10\n```"}
