{"task_id": "Mbpp/579", "solution": "```python\ndef find_dissimilar(tuple1: tuple, tuple2: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the symmetric difference of two tuples.\n\n    Args:\n        tuple1 (tuple): The first input tuple.\n        tuple2 (tuple): The second input tuple.\n    \"\"\"\n    set1 = set(tuple1)\n    set2 = set(tuple2)\n    symmetric_diff_set = (set1 - set2) | (set2 - set1)\n    return tuple(symmetric_diff_set)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/579", "solution": "```python\ndef find_dissimilar(tuple1: tuple, tuple2: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies and returns elements present in one of two input tuples but not in the other.\n    The returned dissimilar elements are sorted in ascending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    set_a = set(tuple1)\n    set_b = set(tuple2)\n\n    elements_only_in_a = set_a - set_b\n    elements_only_in_b = set_b - set_a\n\n    unique_elements = elements_only_in_a.union(elements_only_in_b)\n\n    sorted_dissimilar_list = sorted(list(unique_elements))\n    return tuple(sorted_dissimilar_list)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/580", "solution": "```python\ndef extract_even(input_tuple: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"Processes a nested tuple, extracting even integers while preserving structure.\n    Excludes odd integers and non-integer/non-tuple elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    result_elements = []\n    for element in input_tuple:\n        if isinstance(element, tuple):\n            processed_nested_tuple = extract_even(element)\n            if processed_nested_tuple:\n                result_elements.append(processed_nested_tuple)\n        elif isinstance(element, int):\n            if element % 2 == 0:\n                result_elements.append(element)\n    return tuple(result_elements)\n```"}
