{"task_id": "Mbpp/581", "solution": "import math\n\ndef surface_Area(base_edge, height):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the total surface area of a square pyramid given its base edge and height.\n    This involves computing the slant height and then the sum of the base and lateral face areas.\n    \"\"\"\n    slant_height = math.sqrt(height**2 + (base_edge/2)**2)\n    surface_area = (base_edge * base_edge) + (2 * base_edge * slant_height)\n    return surface_area"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/583", "solution": "```python\ndef _factorial(k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the factorial of a non-negative integer k.\n    This is a helper function for Catalan number calculation.\n    \"\"\"\n    if k == 0:\n        return 1\n    res = 1\n    for i in range(1, k + 1):\n        res *= i\n    return res\n\ndef catalan_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the nth Catalan number using the formula C_n = (2n)! / ((n+1)! * n!).\n    It utilizes an internal helper factorial function for its computations.\n    \"\"\"\n    numerator = _factorial(2 * n)\n    denominator = _factorial(n + 1) * _factorial(n)\n    return numerator // denominator\n```"}
