{"task_id": "Mbpp/597", "solution": "```python\ndef find_kth(array1: list, array2: list, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the k-th smallest element from two given sorted arrays.\n    Uses a two-pointer approach to merge and find the k-th element efficiently.\n    \"\"\"\n    len1, len2 = len(array1), len(array2)\n\n    ptr1 = 0\n    ptr2 = 0\n    current_k = 0\n    result = None\n\n    while ptr1 < len1 and ptr2 < len2:\n        current_k += 1\n        if array1[ptr1] < array2[ptr2]:\n            if current_k == k:\n                result = array1[ptr1]\n                break\n            ptr1 += 1\n        else:\n            if current_k == k:\n                result = array2[ptr2]\n                break\n            ptr2 += 1\n\n    if result is None:\n        # If k-th element not found yet, it must be in the remaining part of array1\n        while ptr1 < len1:\n            current_k += 1\n            if current_k == k:\n                result = array1[ptr1]\n                break\n            ptr1 += 1\n\n    if result is None:\n        # If k-th element not found yet, it must be in the remaining part of array2\n        while ptr2 < len2:\n            current_k += 1\n            if current_k == k:\n                result = array2[ptr2]\n                break\n            ptr2 += 1\n\n    return result\n```\n"}
