{"task_id": "Mbpp/597", "solution": "```python\ndef find_kth(arr1: list[int], arr2: list[int], k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the kth smallest element from two sorted arrays.\n    Assumes inputs are valid as per design specification.\n    \"\"\"\n    n1, n2 = len(arr1), len(arr2)\n    p1, p2 = 0, 0\n    current_element = 0  # Will be updated in each iteration\n\n    # Iterate k times to find the kth smallest element.\n    # k is 1-indexed, so we simulate picking k elements.\n    for _ in range(k):\n        # If arr1 is exhausted, or if arr1[p1] is greater than arr2[p2]\n        # (and arr2 is not exhausted), pick from arr2.\n        if p1 >= n1 or (p2 < n2 and arr2[p2] <= arr1[p1]):\n            current_element = arr2[p2]\n            p2 += 1\n        # Otherwise (arr2 is exhausted, or arr1[p1] is smaller or equal to arr2[p2]),\n        # pick from arr1.\n        else:\n            current_element = arr1[p1]\n            p1 += 1\n\n    return current_element\n```"}
