{"task_id": "Mbpp/608", "solution": "```python\ndef bell_Number(n: int) -> int:\\\n    \"\"\"Calculates the nth Bell number using dynamic programming.\n    It builds a table of Bell numbers and uses precomputed binomial coefficients.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\\\n        return 1\n\n    # Initialize list to store Bell numbers. bell[i] will store B_i.\n    bell = [0] * (n + 1)\n    bell[0] = 1\n\n    # Precompute binomial coefficients (r choose c) using Pascal's triangle.\n    # pascal[r][c] stores the value of (r choose c).\n    pascal = [[0 for _ in range(i + 1)] for i in range(n)]\n    pascal[0][0] = 1\n    for i in range(1, n):\\\n        pascal[i][0] = 1\n        for j in range(1, i):\\\n            pascal[i][j] = pascal[i-1][j-1] + pascal[i-1][j]\n        pascal[i][i] = 1\n\n    # Calculate Bell numbers using the recurrence relation:\n    # B_i = sum_{k=0}^{i-1} (i-1 choose k) * B_k\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\\\n        current_bell = 0\n        for k in range(i):\\\n            current_bell += pascal[i-1][k] * bell[k]\n        bell[i] = current_bell\n\n    return bell[n]\n```"}
