{"task_id": "Mbpp/608", "solution": "```python\ndef bell_Number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Bell number using a dynamic programming approach\n    with a 2D array (Bell triangle).\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0 or n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    # Initialize a 2D list (Bell triangle) of size (n+1) x (n+1) with zeros.\n    bell_triangle = [[0 for _ in range(n + 1)] for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # Base case: The first element of the Bell triangle (B_0) is 1.\n    bell_triangle[0][0] = 1\n\n    # Fill the Bell triangle using the specified recurrence relations.\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        # Set the first element of the current row based on the last element of the previous row.\n        bell_triangle[i][0] = bell_triangle[i-1][i-1]\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            # Calculate elements using the sum of the element above-left and directly left.\n            bell_triangle[i][j] = bell_triangle[i-1][j-1] + bell_triangle[i][j-1]\n\n    # The nth Bell number is the first element of the nth row of the Bell triangle.\n    return bell_triangle[n][0]\n```\n"}
