{"task_id": "Mbpp/612", "solution": "def merge(input_list: list[list[any]]) -> list[list[any]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Transforms a list of two-element sublists into a list of two lists.\n\n    The first returned list contains the first element of each input sublist.\n    The second returned list contains the second element of each input sublist.\n    Elements maintain their original order.\n\n    Args:\n        input_list: A list of lists, where each sublist contains exactly two elements.\n\n    Returns:\n        A list of two lists. The first inner list contains all first elements,\n        and the second inner list contains all second elements from the input.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If input_list is not a list.\n        ValueError: If any sublist does not contain exactly two elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(input_list, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n\n    first_elements = []\n    second_elements = []\n\n    for sublist in input_list:\n        if not isinstance(sublist, list) or len(sublist) != 2:\n            raise ValueError(\"Each sublist must contain exactly two elements.\")\n        first_elements.append(sublist[0])\n        second_elements.append(sublist[1])\n\n    return [first_elements, second_elements]"}
