{"task_id": "Mbpp/620", "solution": "def largest_subset(nums: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the size of the largest subset of numbers where every pair is divisible.\n    It uses dynamic programming after sorting the input numbers.\"\"\"\n    if not nums:\n        return 0\n\n    nums.sort()\n    n = len(nums)\n    dp = [1] * n  # dp[i] stores the size of the largest divisible subset ending with nums[i].\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if nums[i] % nums[j] == 0:\n                dp[i] = max(dp[i], dp[j] + 1)\n\n    return max(dp)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "solution": "```python\ndef get_median(list1: list, list2: list, n: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the median of elements combined from two sorted lists of the same size.\n    It efficiently finds the two middle elements without fully merging the lists.\"\"\"\n    i = 0\n    j = 0\n    m1 = -1\n    m2 = -1\n\n    # Iterate n+1 times to find the n-th and (n+1)-th elements (0-indexed)\n    for count in range(n + 1):\n        m1 = m2\n        if i == n:  # list1 is exhausted\n            m2 = list2[j]\n            j += 1\n        elif j == n:  # list2 is exhausted\n            m2 = list1[i]\n            i += 1\n        elif list1[i] <= list2[j]:\n            m2 = list1[i]\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            m2 = list2[j]\n            j += 1\n\n    return (m1 + m2) / 2.0\n```\n"}
