{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "solution": "```python\nclass List:\n    \"\"\"The List class encapsulates a list of elements.\n    It provides methods for accessing elements and checking its size.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, elements: list[float|int]):\n        self._elements = elements\n        self._size = len(elements)\n\n    def get_element(self, index: int) -> float|int:\n        \"\"\"Returns the element at the specified index.\"\"\"\n        return self._elements[index]\n\n    def get_size(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Returns the number of elements in the list.\"\"\"\n        return self._size\n\n    def is_sorted(self) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Indicates if the list is sorted in ascending order.\n        As per design, we trust the caller's input that lists are sorted.\n        \"\"\"\n        return True\n\nclass MedianCalculator:\n    \"\"\"MedianCalculator computes the median of two List objects.\n    It uses a two-pointer approach to find the median elements efficiently.\n    \"\"\"\n    def calculate_median(self, list1: List, list2: List) -> float:\n        size = list1.get_size()\n        i = 0  # Pointer for list1\n        j = 0  # Pointer for list2\n        m1 = 0.0 # Stores the element at combined_index (size - 1)\n        m2 = 0.0 # Stores the element at combined_index (size)\n\n        # Iterate `size + 1` times to find the two middle elements.\n        # These correspond to indices `size-1` and `size` in the merged list.\n        for count in range(size + 1):\n            if i < size and (j >= size or list1.get_element(i) <= list2.get_element(j)):\n                m1 = m2\n                m2 = float(list1.get_element(i))\n                i += 1\n            else:\n                m1 = m2\n                m2 = float(list2.get_element(j))\n                j += 1\n        return (m1 + m2) / 2.0\n\ndef get_median(list_a_raw: list[float|int], list_b_raw: list[float|int], size: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the median of two sorted lists of the same size.\n    It acts as a facade, creating List objects and delegating the median calculation to MedianCalculator.\n    \"\"\"\n    list1_obj = List(list_a_raw)\n    list2_obj = List(list_b_raw)\n\n    calculator = MedianCalculator()\n    return calculator.calculate_median(list1_obj, list2_obj)\n```"}
