{"task_id": "Mbpp/635", "solution": "def _swap(arr, i, j):\n    \"\"\"Swaps two elements in the list arr at indices i and j.\"\"\"\n    arr[i], arr[j] = arr[j], arr[i]\n\ndef _heapify(arr, n, i):\n    \"\"\"Maintains the max-heap property for a subtree rooted at index i.\"\"\"\n    largest = i\n    l = 2 * i + 1\n    r = 2 * i + 2\n\n    if l < n and arr[l] > arr[largest]:\n        largest = l\n\n    if r < n and arr[r] > arr[largest]:\n        largest = r\n\n    if largest != i:\n        _swap(arr, i, largest)\n        _heapify(arr, n, largest)\n\ndef heap_sort(input_list):\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list using the heap sort algorithm and returns a new sorted list.\"\"\"\n    n = len(input_list)\n    copy_list = list(input_list)\n\n    for i in range(n // 2 - 1, -1, -1):\n        _heapify(copy_list, n, i)\n\n    for i in range(n - 1, 0, -1):\n        _swap(copy_list, 0, i)\n        _heapify(copy_list, i, 0)\n\n    return copy_list"}
