{"task_id": "Mbpp/626", "solution": "def triangle_area(radius: float) -> float | None:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the area of the largest triangle in a semicircle.\n    Returns None if the radius is not positive.\"\"\"\n    if radius <= 0:\n        return None\n\n    # The largest triangle has a base equal to the semicircle's diameter (2 * radius)\n    # and a height equal to the semicircle's radius.\n    # Area = 0.5 * base * height = 0.5 * (2 * radius) * radius\n    area = radius * radius\n\n    return area"}
