{"task_id": "Mbpp/633", "solution": "```python\ndef pair_xor_Sum(numbers: list[int], length: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of XOR operations for all unique pairs in a list of numbers.\n    It iterates through all distinct pairs and accumulates their XOR sum.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_xor_sum = 0\n\n    # Iterate through the list with the outer loop to select the first element of a pair.\n    for i in range(length - 1):\n        # The inner loop selects the second element, ensuring unique pairs by starting from i+1.\n        for j in range(i + 1, length):\n            current_xor = numbers[i] ^ numbers[j]\n            total_xor_sum += current_xor\n\n    return total_xor_sum\n```"}
