{"task_id": "Mbpp/721", "solution": "```python\ndef maxAverageOfPath(matrix: list[list[int]]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a square matrix of size N*N, find a path from the top-left cell\n    to the bottom-right cell moving only right or down, such that the\n    average of the costs of cells in the path is maximized.\n\n    Args:\n        matrix: A square matrix (list of lists) of integer costs.\n\n    Returns:\n        The maximum average cost as a floating-point number.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If the input matrix is empty or not square.\n    \"\"\"\n    N = len(matrix)\n\n    # Validate input matrix\n    if N == 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input matrix cannot be empty.\")\n    for row in matrix:\n        if len(row) != N:\n            raise ValueError(\"Input matrix must be square.\")\n\n    # Initialize a DP table to store the maximum sum to reach each cell\n    dp = [[0] * N for _ in range(N)]\n\n    # Base case: The maximum sum to reach the top-left cell is its own cost\n    dp[0][0] = matrix[0][0]\n\n    # Fill the first row: To reach any cell in the first row,\n    # we can only come from the left.\n    for j in range(1, N):\n        dp[0][j] = matrix[0][j] + dp[0][j-1]\n\n    # Fill the first column: To reach any cell in the first column,\n    # we can only come from above.\n    for i in range(1, N):\n        dp[i][0] = matrix[i][0] + dp[i-1][0]\n\n    # Fill the remaining cells: To reach cell (i, j), we can come from\n    # (i-1, j) (down move) or (i, j-1) (right move).\n    # We choose the path that yields the maximum sum.\n    for i in range(1, N):\n        for j in range(1, N):\n            dp[i][j] = matrix[i][j] + max(dp[i-1][j], dp[i][j-1])\n\n    # The maximum total cost to reach the bottom-right cell\n    max_total_cost = dp[N-1][N-1]\n\n    # The number of cells in any valid path from (0,0) to (N-1, N-1)\n    # in an N*N matrix is always 2*N - 1.\n    num_cells = 2 * N - 1\n\n    # Calculate the maximum average\n    max_average = float(max_total_cost) / num_cells\n\n    return max_average\n```"}
