{"task_id": "Mbpp/726", "solution": "```python\ndef multiply_elements(input_tuple: tuple[int | float]) -> tuple[int | float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the product of adjacent elements in an input tuple of numbers.\n    Returns an empty tuple if the input tuple has fewer than two elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_tuple)\n    if n < 2:\n        return ()\n\n    products = []\n    for i in range(n - 1):\n        products.append(input_tuple[i] * input_tuple[i+1])\n\n    return tuple(products)\n```"}
