{"task_id": "Mbpp/733", "solution": "```python\ndef find_first_occurrence(arr: list[int], num: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the index of the first occurrence of a number in a sorted array using binary search.\n    Returns -1 if the number is not found or the array is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not arr:\n        return -1\n\n    low, high = 0, len(arr) - 1\n    first_occurrence_index = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == num:\n            first_occurrence_index = mid  # Store potential result\n            high = mid - 1               # Continue search in the left half for an earlier occurrence\n        elif arr[mid] < num:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:  # arr[mid] > num\n            high = mid - 1\n\n    return first_occurrence_index\n```"}
