{"task_id": "Mbpp/735", "solution": "```python\ndef _get_msb_pos(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the 0-indexed position of the most significant bit.\n    Assumes number is positive and not zero.\"\"\"\n    return number.bit_length() - 1\n\ndef _get_lsb_pos(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the 0-indexed position of the least significant set bit.\n    Assumes number is positive and not zero.\"\"\"\n    return (number & -number).bit_length() - 1\n\ndef _create_toggle_mask(msb_pos: int, lsb_pos: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Generates a mask with bits set between MSB and LSB positions (exclusive).\n    Returns 0 if no middle bits exist.\"\"\"\n    if msb_pos <= lsb_pos + 1:\n        return 0\n    mask_up_to_msb_minus_1 = (1 << msb_pos) - 1\n    mask_up_to_lsb = (1 << (lsb_pos + 1)) - 1\n    return mask_up_to_msb_minus_1 ^ mask_up_to_lsb\n\ndef toggle_middle_bits(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Toggles bits of an integer, excluding its most significant and least significant bits.\n    Returns the original number unchanged if it has two or fewer bits.\"\"\"\n    if number.bit_length() <= 2:\n        return number\n\n    msb_pos = _get_msb_pos(number)\n    lsb_pos = _get_lsb_pos(number)\n    toggle_mask = _create_toggle_mask(msb_pos, lsb_pos)\n\n    return number ^ toggle_mask\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/736", "solution": "```python\ndef left_insertion(arr: list, x: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Locates the left insertion point for a specified value in a sorted list.\n    This function behaves like `bisect_left` from Python's `bisect` module.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(arr)\n\n    while low < high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if arr[mid] < x:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid\n    return low\n```"}
