{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Any\n\ndef rotate_right(input_list: List[Any], n: int) -> List[Any]:\n    \"\"\"Rotates a list to the right by n positions, returning a new rotated list.\n    Handles edge cases for empty lists or zero rotation count efficiently.\"\"\"\n    length = len(input_list)\n\n    if length == 0 or n == 0:\n        return input_list\n\n    effective_n = n % length\n    split_point = length - effective_n\n\n    part1 = input_list[0:split_point]\n    part2 = input_list[split_point:length]\n\n    rotated_list = part2 + part1\n\n    return rotated_list\n```"}
