{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "```python\ndef rotate_right(input_list: list, n: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates a given list to the right by a specified number of items.\n    The rotation handles various values of n, including those larger than list length or negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    list_length = len(input_list)\n\n    if list_length == 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Calculate the effective rotation amount using the modulo operator.\n    # This correctly handles cases where n is greater than the list length, negative, or zero.\n    n = n % list_length\n\n    # Split the list into two parts and concatenate them to form the rotated list.\n    # The last 'n' elements of the original list become the first part of the rotated list.\n    rotated_part = input_list[list_length - n:]\n    remaining_part = input_list[:list_length - n]\n\n    return rotated_part + remaining_part\n```"}
