{"task_id": "Mbpp/748", "solution": "```python\ndef capital_words_spaces(input_string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Inserts spaces between words starting with capital letters in a given string.\n    It handles camelCase and PascalCase conventions to segment words.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_string:\n        return \"\"\n\n    result_chars = [input_string[0]]\n    for i in range(1, len(input_string)):\n        current_char = input_string[i]\n        prev_char = input_string[i - 1]\n\n        # Insert space for 'camelCase' (lowercase followed by uppercase)\n        if prev_char.islower() and current_char.isupper():\n            result_chars.append(' ')\n        # Insert space for 'PascalCase' where a sequence of capitals is broken by a new word\n        # (uppercase followed by uppercase, then by lowercase, e.g., HTTPRequest -> HTTP Request)\n        elif (prev_char.isupper() and\n              current_char.isupper() and\n              i + 1 < len(input_string) and\n              input_string[i + 1].islower()):\n            result_chars.append(' ')\n\n        result_chars.append(current_char)\n\n    return \"\".join(result_chars)\n```\n"}
