{"task_id": "Mbpp/759", "solution": "```python\ndef is_decimal(input_string: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the input string represents a decimal number with exactly two decimal places.\n    This function validates the string format against a specific numeric pattern.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_string:\n        return False\n\n    s = input_string\n    # Handle optional leading sign\n    if s[0] == '+' or s[0] == '-':\n        s = s[1:]\n\n    if not s:  # String was just a sign or empty after sign removal\n        return False\n\n    parts = s.split('.')\n\n    # Must have exactly one decimal point to split into two parts\n    if len(parts) != 2:\n        return False\n\n    integer_part = parts[0]\n    decimal_part = parts[1]\n\n    # Validate integer part: must have at least one digit and all digits\n    if not integer_part: # Handles cases like \".11\"\n        return False\n    for char in integer_part:\n        if not ('0' <= char <= '9'):\n            return False\n\n    # Validate decimal part: must have exactly two digits and all digits\n    if len(decimal_part) != 2:\n        return False\n    for char in decimal_part:\n        if not ('0' <= char <= '9'):\n            return False\n\n    return True\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/759", "solution": "```python\ndef is_decimal(input_string: str) -> bool:\n    # Checks if the string is a decimal number with exactly two decimal places.\n    # Handles optional leading signs and validates character types and structure.\n\n    if not input_string:\n        return False\n\n    s = input_string\n    # Remove leading sign if present.\n    if s[0] == '+' or s[0] == '-':\n        s = s[1:]\n\n    # If the string is empty after sign removal (e.g., just \"+\"), it's invalid.\n    if not s:\n        return False\n\n    # The string must contain exactly one decimal point for 'exactly 2 decimal places'.\n    if s.count('.') != 1:\n        return False\n\n    # Split into integer and fractional parts.\n    parts = s.split('.')\n    integer_part = parts[0]\n    fractional_part = parts[1]\n\n    # Validate that both parts contain only digits. An empty integer part is valid (e.g., \".11\").\n    if not (integer_part == '' or integer_part.isdigit()):\n        return False\n\n    if not fractional_part.isdigit():\n        return False\n\n    # Ensure the fractional part has precisely two digits.\n    return len(fractional_part) == 2\n```"}
