{"task_id": "Mbpp/763", "solution": "```python\ndef find_min_diff(array: tuple | list, size: int) -> int | float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the minimum absolute difference between any two elements in a given array.\n    Returns float('inf') if the array has fewer than two elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if size < 2:\n        return float('inf')\n\n    # Sort the array to efficiently find minimum differences between adjacent elements.\n    sorted_array = sorted(array)\n\n    min_diff = float('inf')\n\n    # Iterate through the sorted array to find the minimum difference.\n    for i in range(size - 1):\n        current_diff = abs(sorted_array[i+1] - sorted_array[i])\n        if current_diff < min_diff:\n            min_diff = current_diff\n\n    return min_diff\n```"}
