{"task_id": "Mbpp/767", "solution": "```python\ndef get_pairs_count(numbers: list[int], target_sum: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts distinct pairs of elements in a list whose sum equals a target value.\n\n    Pairs are identified by their unique indices (i, j) where j > i.\n    \"\"\"\n    pair_count = 0\n    n = len(numbers)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            if numbers[i] + numbers[j] == target_sum:\n                pair_count += 1\n    return pair_count\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/770", "solution": "```python\ndef odd_num_sum(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of the fourth powers of the first n odd natural numbers.\n    Assumes n is a positive integer based on critical requirements.\n    \"\"\"\n    running_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        current_odd_number = 2 * i + 1\n        fourth_power = current_odd_number ** 4\n        running_sum += fourth_power\n    return running_sum\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/770", "solution": "```python\ndef odd_num_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of the fourth power of the first 'n' odd natural numbers.\n    It iterates 'n' times, computing (2*k-1)^4 for each k from 1 to n.\n    \"\"\"\n    current_sum = 0\n    for k in range(1, n + 1):\n        odd_num = (2 * k - 1)\n        fourth_power = odd_num ** 4\n        current_sum += fourth_power\n    return current_sum\n```"}
