{"task_id": "Mbpp/769", "solution": "def Diff(list1: list, list2: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the set difference between two lists, returning unique elements from list1 not in list2.\n    The order of elements in the result is based on their first appearance in list1.\"\"\"\n\n    list2_set = set(list2)\n\n    result_list = []\n    seen_in_result = set()\n\n    for item in list1:\n        if item not in list2_set and item not in seen_in_result:\n            result_list.append(item)\n            seen_in_result.add(item)\n\n    return result_list"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/771", "solution": "```python\ndef check_expression(expression: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given expression has balanced parentheses, brackets, and braces.\n    Returns True if balanced, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    OPENING_BRACKETS = {'(', '{', '['}\n    BRACKET_MAP = {')': '(', '}': '{', ']': '['}\n\n    stack = []\n\n    for char in expression:\n        if char in OPENING_BRACKETS:\n            stack.append(char)\n        elif char in BRACKET_MAP:  # char is a closing bracket\n            if not stack:\n                return False\n\n            last_open = stack.pop()\n            if BRACKET_MAP[char] != last_open:\n                return False\n        # Ignore other characters as per design\n\n    return not stack\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/771", "solution": "```python\ndef check_expression(expression_string: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if the given expression has balanced opening and closing delimiters.\n    Uses a stack to track opening delimiters and ensures proper matching.\n    \"\"\"\n    stack = []\n\n    opening_delimiters = \"([{\"\n    closing_delimiters = \")]}\"\n\n    # Map each closing delimiter to its corresponding opening delimiter\n    matching_pairs = {\n        ')': '(',\n        ']': '[',\n        '}': '{'\n    }\n\n    for char in expression_string:\n        if char in opening_delimiters:\n            stack.append(char)\n        elif char in closing_delimiters:\n            if not stack:\n                return False  # Closing delimiter found with no matching opening delimiter\n\n            last_open = stack.pop()\n\n            # Check if the popped opening delimiter matches the current closing delimiter\n            if matching_pairs[char] != last_open:\n                return False  # Mismatch between opening and closing delimiters\n        # Non-delimiter characters are ignored\n\n    # The expression is balanced if and only if the stack is empty at the end\n    return not stack\n```\n"}
