{"task_id": "Mbpp/772", "solution": "```python\n# The WordProcessor component encapsulates word manipulation logic.\nclass WordProcessor:\n    @staticmethod\n    def split_words(text: str) -> list[str]:\n        \"\"\"Splits the input string into a list of words using spaces as delimiters.\"\"\"\n        return text.split()\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def filter_words(words: list[str], k: int) -> list[str]:\n        \"\"\"Filters words, keeping only those whose length is not equal to k.\"\"\"\n        return [word for word in words if len(word) != k]\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def join_words(words: list[str]) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Joins a list of words into a single string, separated by single spaces.\"\"\"\n        return ' '.join(words)\n\ndef remove_length(input_string: str, k: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Removes all words of a specified length k from the input string.\n    Punctuation is considered part of a word when calculating its length.\n    \"\"\"\n    words = WordProcessor.split_words(input_string)\n    filtered_words = WordProcessor.filter_words(words, k)\n    modified_string = WordProcessor.join_words(filtered_words)\n    return modified_string\n```\n"}
