{"task_id": "Mbpp/781", "solution": "```python\ndef count_divisors(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks whether the count of divisors for a positive integer is even.\n\n    Args:\n        number: A positive integer (N > 0).\n\n    Returns:\n        True if the count of divisors is even, False otherwise.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If the input number is not a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input number must be a positive integer (N > 0).\")\n\n    def _calculate_divisor_count(n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the total number of divisors for a positive integer.\"\"\"\n        count = 0\n        i = 1\n        while i * i <= n:\n            if n % i == 0:\n                if i * i == n:\n                    count += 1\n                else:\n                    count += 2\n            i += 1\n        return count\n\n    divisor_count = _calculate_divisor_count(number)\n    return divisor_count % 2 == 0\n```"}
