{"task_id": "Mbpp/786", "solution": "```python\ndef right_insertion(sorted_list: list[any], value: any) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Locates the right insertion point for a value in a sorted list using binary search.\n    This ensures all elements before the index are <= value, and all after are > value.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(sorted_list)\n    # ans will store the smallest index i such that sorted_list[i] > value\n    ans = high\n\n    while low < high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if sorted_list[mid] > value:\n            # If sorted_list[mid] is greater, then mid is a potential answer,\n            # and we might find an even smaller index to its left.\n            ans = mid\n            high = mid\n        else:\n            # If sorted_list[mid] is less than or equal, the insertion point must be to its right.\n            low = mid + 1\n\n    return ans\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/786", "solution": "```python\ndef right_insertion(sorted_list, value_to_insert):\n    \"\"\"\n    Locates the right insertion point for a value in a sorted list.\n    The function ensures the new value is placed after any existing occurrences.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(sorted_list)\n\n    while low < high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if sorted_list[mid] <= value_to_insert:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid\n    return low\n```"}
