{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "```python\ndef last(sorted_array: list[int], element: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the last position of an element in a sorted array.\n    Returns the 0-based index of the last occurrence, or -1 if not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    low, high = 0, len(sorted_array) - 1\n    last_found_index = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if sorted_array[mid] == element:\n            last_found_index = mid\n            low = mid + 1  # Continue searching in the right half for a later occurrence\n        elif sorted_array[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return last_found_index\n```"}
