{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "```python\ndef last(array: list[int], element: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the last position (index) of a specified element in a given sorted array using binary search.\n    Returns the highest index (0-based) or -1 if the element is not found.\n\n    Example:\n        >>> last([1,2,3], 1)\n        0\n        >>> last([1,2,2,3,4], 2)\n        2\n        >>> last([5,5,5,5], 5)\n        3\n        >>> last([1,2,3], 4)\n        -1\n    \"\"\"\n    low, high = 0, len(array) - 1\n    result = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if array[mid] == element:\n            result = mid\n            low = mid + 1\n        elif array[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result\n```\n"}
