{"task_id": "Mbpp/784", "solution": "```python\ndef mul_even_odd(input_list: list[int]) -> int | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the product of the first even and first odd numbers found in a list.\n    Returns None if either number is not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    first_odd = None\n    first_even = None\n\n    for number in input_list:\n        if first_odd is None and number % 2 != 0:\n            first_odd = number\n        if first_even is None and number % 2 == 0:\n            first_even = number\n\n        if first_odd is not None and first_even is not None:\n            break  # Stop early once both are found\n\n    if first_odd is not None and first_even is not None:\n        return first_odd * first_even\n    else:\n        return None\n```"}
