{"task_id": "Mbpp/797", "solution": "```python\ndef sum_in_range(l: int, r: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of all odd natural numbers within the inclusive range [l, r].\n    Natural numbers are integers greater than 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    # Ensure iteration starts from at least 1, as natural numbers are greater than 0.\n    start_num = max(1, l)\n    for num in range(start_num, r + 1):\n        if num % 2 != 0:\n            total_sum += num\n    return total_sum\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/797", "solution": "```python\ndef sum_in_range(l, r):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of all odd natural numbers within the inclusive range [l, r].\"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    for number in range(l, r + 1):\n        if number > 0 and number % 2 != 0:\n            total_sum += number\n    return total_sum\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "```python\ndef left_rotate(number: int, rotation_amount: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Performs a left bit rotation on a 32-bit integer.\n    The rotation amount is normalized modulo 32.\n    \"\"\"\n    d = rotation_amount % 32\n\n    # Calculate the left-shifted part and the wrapped-around part, then combine them.\n    rotated_num = (number << d) | (number >> (32 - d))\n\n    # Mask the result to ensure it stays within 32 bits.\n    return rotated_num & 0xFFFFFFFF\n```"}
