{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "```python\ndef left_rotate(number: int, d: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates the bits of a given 32-bit number to the left by d bits.\n\n    Args:\n        number: The 32-bit integer to rotate.\n        d: The number of bits to rotate left.\n\n    Returns:\n        The 32-bit integer result after the left bitwise rotation.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Normalize d to be within the range [0, 31] for 32-bit rotation.\n    d = d % 32\n    # Perform the left rotation using bitwise shifts and OR operation.\n    # The final result is masked with 0xFFFFFFFF to ensure it remains a 32-bit integer.\n    return ((number << d) | (number >> (32 - d))) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n\n```"}
