{"task_id": "Mbpp/804", "solution": "```python\ndef is_product_even(numbers: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the product of numbers in the input list is an even integer.\n    Handles empty lists, zero, negative numbers, and floating-point numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not numbers:\n        return False\n\n    # Initialize product as a float to consistently handle all subsequent multiplications,\n    # and to allow using the .is_integer() method on the final result.\n    current_product = 1.0\n\n    for num in numbers:\n        # If any number in the list is 0, the overall product will be 0, which is an even integer.\n        if num == 0:\n            return True\n        current_product *= num\n\n    # After calculating the product, check if it's an integer-like float (e.g., 6.0)\n    # and then determine its parity.\n    if current_product.is_integer():\n        # If the product is an integer (e.g., 6.0, 3.0), convert it to an int for reliable modulo operation.\n        return int(current_product) % 2 == 0\n    else:\n        # If the product is a non-integer float (e.g., 4.5), it cannot be an even integer.\n        return False\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/806", "solution": "```python\ndef max_run_uppercase(input_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum length of a consecutive run of uppercase characters.\n    Returns 0 if the string is empty or contains no uppercase characters.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_string:\n        return 0\n\n    max_run_length = 0\n    current_run_length = 0\n\n    for char in input_string:\n        if char.isupper():\n            current_run_length += 1\n        else:\n            max_run_length = max(max_run_length, current_run_length)\n            current_run_length = 0\n\n    # Final check to account for a run ending at the end of the string\n    max_run_length = max(max_run_length, current_run_length)\n\n    return max_run_length\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/806", "solution": "```python\ndef max_run_uppercase(input_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum contiguous run of uppercase characters in a string.\n    Handles empty strings and strings with no uppercase characters by returning 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_run = 0\n    current_run = 0\n\n    for char in input_string:\n        if char.isupper():\n            current_run += 1\n        else:\n            max_run = max(max_run, current_run)\n            current_run = 0\n\n    # Final check for any trailing uppercase run\n    max_run = max(max_run, current_run)\n\n    return max_run\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/805", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef max_sum_list(list_of_lists: List[List[int]]) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the inner list from a list of lists whose sum of elements is the highest.\n    Returns an empty list if the input list_of_lists is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not list_of_lists:\n        return []\n\n    highest_sum = float('-inf')\n    highest_sum_inner_list: List[int] = []\n\n    for inner_list in list_of_lists:\n        current_sum = sum(inner_list)\n\n        if current_sum > highest_sum:\n            highest_sum = current_sum\n            highest_sum_inner_list = inner_list\n\n    return highest_sum_inner_list\n```"}
